    "abstract": "The online version contains supplementary material available at 10.1007/s13593-026-01091-0.",
    "field": "Crop growth modelling",
    "problem": "Existing crop phenology prediction models for future climates commonly neglect uncertainties arising from the climate scenario data and its interaction with the model, considering only the phenology model itself as a source of uncertainty, which leads to inaccurate predictions.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a dynamic crop phenology model framework that combines environmental covariates using additive dose-response curves and selects the optimal model by simultaneously minimizing uncertainties arising from both ground-truth observations and future climate scenario data.",
    "task": "The task is to develop a model framework to reduce uncertainty in future crop phenology predictions by simultaneously optimizing for uncertainties arising from the phenology model, climate scenario data, and their interaction.",
